00:20:32.830 --> 00:20:34.920
Turn back and make an immediate landing

00:20:34.920 --> 00:20:39.180
The demolition truck will remove a bag containing a bomb from your luggage compartment

00:20:39.180 --> 00:20:41.070
The bag is black leather

00:20:41.070 --> 00:20:43.660
Claim check number 4720

00:20:43.660 --> 00:20:47.100
Repeat, claim check number 4720

00:20:47.100 --> 00:21:00.000
Attention everyone, this...

00:21:00.320 --> 00:21:06.660
emergency. All personnel is ordered off the runways and field. All others please

00:21:06.660 --> 00:21:13.810
remain within administration building. I repeat, this is an emergency. What's going

00:21:13.810 --> 00:21:16.640
on? Come on, I know the manager. Let's find out.

00:21:19.720 --> 00:21:23.480
Alfredo, what's happened? That's the idiot. Smuggled a time bomb aboard a plane.

00:21:23.720 --> 00:21:30.000
Which plane? Flight 217. Flight 2... Bad. Boy, you... Hold it, Jerry. Hold it.

00:21:30.510 --> 00:21:32.370
Anything happens to Pam?

00:22:00.920 --> 00:22:01.980
They have to make it.

00:22:06.950 --> 00:22:28.320
Let's go, Jerry. Let's get out there.

00:23:01.530 --> 00:23:10.760
Atencion, por favor. El peligro ha pasado. Atencion, por favor. El peligro ha pasado.

00:23:12.210 --> 00:23:21.740
Attention, everyone. The danger has passed. All clear. Attention, everyone. All clear.

00:23:21.820 --> 00:23:24.100
Well, guess I better get back to my plane.

00:23:24.320 --> 00:23:26.630
Oh, man. Nothing doing. You're staying with me.

00:23:27.290 --> 00:23:29.810
Leave me one thing while I was waiting for that plane to come down.

00:23:30.060 --> 00:23:32.220
Anything I can do, we can do better.

00:23:32.500 --> 00:23:32.980
Together.

00:23:33.600 --> 00:23:34.700
Jerry, you're sweet.

00:23:34.900 --> 00:23:35.600
Oh, darling.

00:23:36.960 --> 00:23:38.920
Shall we look for the taxi driver?

00:23:41.060 --> 00:23:50.580
All yours, officer.

00:23:52.840 --> 00:23:54.540
Now, come on, let's see what blew up.

00:23:59.450 --> 00:24:00.000
Come on.

00:24:03.160 --> 00:24:05.980
No, that bomb, they must have given me the wrong suitcase.

00:24:06.280 --> 00:24:08.420
Oh, my God, who is your father in my car?

00:24:08.800 --> 00:24:10.400
Oh, what a shame.

00:24:10.930 --> 00:24:12.340
It's a tough break, amigo.

00:24:12.780 --> 00:24:16.340
Yes, because I was the fastest driver of all over Mexico.

00:24:17.890 --> 00:24:19.930
What's so funny? What's he saying?

00:24:20.470 --> 00:24:22.410
Maybe it isn't for mixed company, Jerry.

00:24:22.770 --> 00:24:24.650
Oh, no. This may surprise you, though.

00:24:25.180 --> 00:24:27.360
The driver is very happy. He's very proud.

00:24:27.690 --> 00:24:27.910
What?

00:24:28.850 --> 00:24:30.000
Yes, he says that for just...

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:34.880
Just one little moment, he owned the fastest moving taxicab in all of Mexico City.

00:24:34.880 --> 00:24:37.000
Oh, that's wonderful!

00:24:37.000 --> 00:24:53.380
"Mr. and Miss North" is directed by Lou Landers, produced by John W. Lovedon.

00:24:53.380 --> 00:25:00.000
A John W. Lovedon production, starring Barbara Britton and Richard Denning.

00:25:00.510 --> 00:25:02.190
Featuring Francis DeSales.

00:25:03.780 --> 00:25:15.000
This has been a film presentation.
